  <h2 style="margin-top: 28px;">Sunrise, then down</h2>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    The night before, I'd been stressed. Four miles of snow downhill, a two-hour drive, a noon call, a 1:30, a flight. I wrote out a schedule on a notepad until I felt calm about it.
  </p>

  <img loading="lazy"
    src="/images/park-butte/notepad-plan.jpg"
    alt="Handwritten schedule on a GFiber notepad: 'impossible to say in one sentence. But I know I have time & I can be calm.'"
    style="width: 100%; max-width: 380px; border-radius: 10px; margin: 12px 0 20px 0;"
  />

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    I was up before 5. The teenagers had cell service somehow, so I FaceTimed my parents before I started down. The snow on the way down was sketchy in a few spots, but manageable. I made it back to the car at 8 — right on time, maybe a little early. I had planned it to the minute and then just executed it.
  </p>

  <img loading="lazy"
    src="/images/park-butte/lookout-morning-smiling.jpg"
    alt="Morning in the lookout — smiling in a sleeping bag with Baker through the window"
    style="width: 100%; max-width: 500px; border-radius: 10px; margin: 20px 0 12px 0;"
  />

